Here is the UI for the Premium Leather Jacket product details page. 

First, we will initialize the surface and set up the default values for size and color inside the data model.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9",
  "createSurface": {
    "surfaceId": "main",
    "catalogId": "https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/catalogs/basic/catalog.json"
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

Next, we initialize the data model to have pre-selected values for size and color.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9",
  "updateDataModel": {
    "surfaceId": "main",
    "path": "/",
    "value": {
      "selectedSize": ["M"],
      "selectedColor": ["Black"]
    }
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

Finally, we construct the product details page using a horizontal layout (`Row`) featuring product media on the left, and metadata & configurations on the right.

