Here is the flow to initialize the surface, populate the user's logged-in profile data, and render the profile UI.

### Step 1: Create the Surface
First, we initialize the surface `'main'` using the basic catalog.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9",
  "createSurface": {
    "surfaceId": "main",
    "catalogId": "https://a2ui.org/specification/v0_9/catalogs/basic/catalog.json"
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

### Step 2: Populate the Data Model
Next, we populate the client-side data model with the user's profile information. This single update sets the name to `"John Doe"` and the email to `"john.doe@example.com"` under the `/user` path.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9",
  "updateDataModel": {
    "surfaceId": "main",
    "path": "/",
    "value": {
      "user": {
        "name": "John Doe",
        "email": "john.doe@example.com"
      }
    }
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

### Step 3: Render the Profile UI
Finally, we update the component tree to display this newly loaded profile data using standard text formatting templates bound directly to the data model.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9",
  "updateComponents": {
    "surfaceId": "main",
    "components": [
      {
        "id": "root",
        "component": "Column",
        "children": [
          "title",
          "name_display",
          "email_display"
        ],
        "align": "start"
      },
      {
        "id": "title",
        "component": "Text",
        "text": "User Profile",
        "variant": "h2"
      },
      {
        "id": "name_display",
        "component": "Text",
        "text": {
          "call": "formatString",
          "args": {
            "value": "Name: ${/user/name}"
          },
          "returnType": "string"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "email_display",
        "component": "Text",
        "text": {
          "call": "formatString",
          "args": {
            "value": "Email: ${/user/email}"
          },
          "returnType": "string"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

